From d3e4b2e2b912787a7f471768007930d0aaf6bcc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:34:29 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): the gateway delivers legacy tui notices for
 chats it owns through the local FIFO

A Desktop chat's kanban subs are platform='tui', claimable only by the legacy
Desktop backend. Once the chat's turns run on the canonical gateway (LOCAL route),
that backend is refused SESSION_NOT_OWNED and rewinds with up-to-300s backoff,
while the gateway collector skipped tui rows (no tui adapter). Notices waited for
the gateway's whole busy chain: 64 min for chat 20261026_235722_bef6c6 on
2026-11-11 (t_01a1ce31dbbb74bd).

The gateway now claims a tui row only when it would make the legacy backend
refuse: a live LOCAL session for the chat (compression lineage aware) whose
ledger holds forwardable work or whose turn lease this process holds, no local
sibling row for the same card. Delivery is a FIFO kanban wake via
admit_route_wake after re-checking the live route; every refusal or error
rewinds the claim (never Platform('tui') -> advance, never a sub drop). Cursor
key stays tui. [daveey]
